WEBVTT

00:04.610 --> 00:06.480
This feels amazing...

00:07.490 --> 00:10.970
<i>The plan was to work quietly and 
inconspicuously as an underground healer,</i>

00:10.970 --> 00:14.990
<i>but things sure got noisier than I expected.</i>

00:15.360 --> 00:18.740
<i>It's been a long time since I've 
had a chance to relax by myself.</i>

00:19.190 --> 00:21.550
I'm glad I came here.

00:38.010 --> 00:45.560
<b>The Brilliant Healer's
New Life in the Shadows</b>

01:53.740 --> 01:59.290
The investigation into the mastermind behind 
the golem attack hasn't revealed much.

01:59.290 --> 02:05.520
All I've been able to confirm is that it's an 
individual who calls himself "The Guide."

02:05.520 --> 02:06.790
I see.

02:07.330 --> 02:08.930
"The Guide"...

02:08.930 --> 02:11.730
I'm going to remember that name.

02:11.730 --> 02:14.110
And one day, I'm going to collect from him.

02:14.550 --> 02:17.950
There wasn't much of a 
trail to follow, either.

02:17.950 --> 02:21.840
The location where they met with that 
man, Aston, was already abandoned,

02:21.840 --> 02:23.870
with no trace left behind.

02:24.370 --> 02:26.750
I did some digging myself.

02:26.750 --> 02:29.450
The guy only started visiting 
the Underground Guild recently,

02:29.450 --> 02:32.500
and he tended to be alone.

02:32.760 --> 02:36.170
Lynga heard the same kind of story.

02:36.170 --> 02:40.390
In the underworld, the standard is to avoid 
prying into each other's backgrounds.

02:40.390 --> 02:43.760
I think there's a limit to what can 
be learned from questioning people.

02:43.760 --> 02:47.520
The Royal Knights will be pursuing 
him as a dangerous individual,

02:47.520 --> 02:50.110
but considering how thoroughly 
he erased his trail,

02:50.110 --> 02:52.860
it's likely he won't resurface for a while.

02:53.340 --> 02:54.730
I see.

02:55.290 --> 02:57.840
But he'll come back sooner or later.

02:57.840 --> 02:59.990
That's the impression I get.

02:59.990 --> 03:04.370
Yeah. I think this Guide 
still has some scheme going.

03:04.370 --> 03:07.150
He won't be simple to deal 
with, that's for sure.

03:07.150 --> 03:10.370
He may have ties even 
deeper in the underworld.

03:10.370 --> 03:14.610
I'd appreciate it if you demihumans 
didn't randomly speculate.

03:14.610 --> 03:17.500
Haven't you been mostly guessing yourself?

03:17.500 --> 03:22.400
I appreciate your help from 
the other day, but no.

03:22.400 --> 03:25.020
My guesses are not simply guesses,

03:25.020 --> 03:28.020
but speculation informed by my 
investigation and experience.

03:28.020 --> 03:29.520
Hang on a second.

03:29.520 --> 03:33.270
Could you all stop talking at each 
other from across the room?

03:33.270 --> 03:34.980
It's kind of awkward.

03:34.980 --> 03:37.280
Th-There's nothing that can be done.

03:37.280 --> 03:39.070
Given my position as a Royal Knight,

03:39.070 --> 03:42.860
I can hardly be seen sipping tea at the 
same table as a group of demihumans.

03:42.860 --> 03:45.370
Like we'd even want you at our table.

03:45.370 --> 03:46.740
Okay, settle down.

03:46.740 --> 03:49.120
No fighting in the clinic!

03:49.120 --> 03:51.500
Besides, I'm taking today 
off because I'm tired!

03:51.500 --> 03:54.140
So if you're not an 
emergency patient, get out!

03:58.290 --> 03:59.770
Hey, Zenos...

04:03.260 --> 04:06.700
I had an idea.

04:06.700 --> 04:08.140
You did?

04:08.400 --> 04:12.270
Yeah. You've seemed really 
tired since the golem attack,

04:12.270 --> 04:15.580
so I thought about what 
might make you feel better.

04:15.580 --> 04:20.730
So maybe... for a change of pace... 
the two of us could... go...

04:20.730 --> 04:22.740
Go... where?

04:24.240 --> 04:25.740
You and I could go to a hot—

04:25.740 --> 04:26.990
Doc!

04:28.070 --> 04:30.120
What's up? Forget something?

04:30.120 --> 04:32.170
Actually, I have a proposal.

04:32.170 --> 04:33.210
A proposal?

04:34.430 --> 04:37.380
Well, that golem mess was 
a real nightmare, right?

04:37.730 --> 04:39.720
How about we head to a hot spring?

04:39.720 --> 04:41.010
A hot spring?

04:41.010 --> 04:44.060
I was thinking it could 
help you recover a bit!

04:44.060 --> 04:45.130
I see...

04:45.130 --> 04:47.600
That might make for a nice change of pace.

04:47.600 --> 04:49.010
Awesome!

04:49.010 --> 04:50.580
It's a promise, Doc.

04:54.770 --> 04:58.110
What? You forget something?

04:58.470 --> 04:59.760
Nope!

04:59.760 --> 05:02.350
Lynga has a brilliant idea!

05:02.350 --> 05:03.740
Oh, you do?

05:05.570 --> 05:08.370
The golem attack was tough for all of us...

05:08.370 --> 05:10.470
So let's go to a hot spring!

05:10.470 --> 05:11.870
A hot spring?

05:11.870 --> 05:13.590
It doesn't sound bad, but—

05:12.520 --> 05:13.590
Great!

05:13.590 --> 05:15.620
It's a promise, Sir Zenos!

05:19.000 --> 05:20.420
Zenos! I think—

05:20.420 --> 05:23.070
A hot spring, right?! You didn't forget 
anything! You just wanna go to a hot spring!

05:23.070 --> 05:24.380
That's it, isn't it?!

05:24.380 --> 05:26.510
H-How did you know?

05:26.510 --> 05:28.170
We must truly be of one heart!

05:28.170 --> 05:30.540
You and the other girls, maybe!

05:30.540 --> 05:32.390
No wonder you get along!

05:35.820 --> 05:38.850
M-Mr. Zenos, I wanted to ask you...

05:38.850 --> 05:42.050
Hot springs, right?! You wanna 
go to a hot spring, too, don't you?!

05:42.050 --> 05:43.480
Sounds like fun!

05:45.490 --> 05:48.380
Why are they all so 
obsessed with hot springs?

05:49.270 --> 05:51.740
Anyway, what did you want to talk about, Lily?

05:52.880 --> 05:55.250
Never mind! Just... never mind!

05:57.510 --> 06:04.180
How amusing to see your effort to outdo your 
rivals undercut by all of them in the same fashion.

06:04.180 --> 06:08.260
I never tire of watching the unseemly 
struggles of women in love.

06:08.260 --> 06:10.400
It's occurred to me

06:10.400 --> 06:14.140
that for the highest class of undead, 
your tastes are kind of vulgar.

06:14.140 --> 06:17.670
And I certainly haven't been to 
a hot spring in a long time!

06:17.670 --> 06:19.520
Wait, you're coming, too?

06:24.480 --> 06:26.490
This is the men's bath.

06:26.490 --> 06:27.990
I know.

06:27.990 --> 06:31.240
It'll be fine. I put a sign up 
that says it's being cleaned.

06:31.240 --> 06:32.240
Wh-Whoa!

06:34.320 --> 06:37.240
My inclination is to get 
a little more aggressive,

06:37.240 --> 06:39.380
but I don't want to turn you against me.

06:39.880 --> 06:40.930
I see...

06:41.800 --> 06:46.260
Y'know, my brother and underlings 
have said I seem different lately.

06:46.260 --> 06:49.260
You do seem calmer.

06:49.260 --> 06:53.980
I never dreamed I'd get along 
with werewolves and orcs,

06:53.980 --> 06:56.790
much less chat with a Royal Knight.

06:57.600 --> 07:01.020
I think you might just change the world, Doc.

07:02.020 --> 07:03.450
You're exaggerating.

07:03.450 --> 07:06.120
I'm just an underground healer 
at a run-down clinic.

07:07.050 --> 07:07.990
Hey...

07:08.270 --> 07:09.230
What is it?

07:09.990 --> 07:12.380
Why are you getting closer and closer?

07:12.380 --> 07:13.890
You noticed, huh?

07:13.890 --> 07:16.480
I was hoping the conversation would 
get you to lower your guard.

07:16.480 --> 07:19.000
I was stupid for expecting 
this to go normally!

07:20.110 --> 07:22.000
Hold it right there!

07:22.000 --> 07:24.250
Zophia! No fair getting a head start!

07:25.370 --> 07:26.960
This is the men's bath!

07:26.960 --> 07:28.570
What's wrong with you?

07:28.570 --> 07:29.760
What's wrong with <i>you</i>?

07:29.760 --> 07:33.010
Lynga is simply dizzy from the heat!

07:33.010 --> 07:34.140
That's clearly a lie.

07:35.510 --> 07:39.270
All of the dizziness has Lynga falling over!

07:40.390 --> 07:46.610
Let go, Zophia! Lynga is on the 
verge of fainting into Zenos's arms!

07:46.610 --> 07:49.740
If you're about to faint, 
why are you still so strong?!

07:49.740 --> 07:51.380
Quit fussing, you two!

07:51.380 --> 07:53.360
Settle down, and more importantly, get out!

07:53.360 --> 07:54.680
Hold it!

07:54.680 --> 07:56.990
I won't have you forget about me!

07:56.990 --> 07:58.740
What were you even doing in there?!

08:00.230 --> 08:03.000
I was waiting in the water for you, Zenos!

08:03.000 --> 08:04.080
What do you think?

08:04.080 --> 08:06.720
Is my body not, as they say, bodacious?

08:06.720 --> 08:08.480
It's kinda too dark to tell.

08:08.480 --> 08:10.510
That wasn't an invitation 
to come closer, okay?

08:11.590 --> 08:13.070
You're not going anywhere!

08:13.070 --> 08:15.390
Lynga is even more bodacious!

08:18.260 --> 08:20.620
Enough!

08:20.620 --> 08:23.390
What do you demihumans think you're doing?!

08:23.390 --> 08:25.200
This is the men's bath!

08:25.200 --> 08:27.480
Have you no shame at all?!

08:27.480 --> 08:29.980
Then what are <i>you</i> doing in here?

08:29.980 --> 08:32.990
You're here to see Zenos, too, aren't you?

08:33.620 --> 08:39.870
N-No! I just got lost and mistook 
the men's bath for the women's!

08:39.870 --> 08:41.380
Great, more competition.

08:41.380 --> 08:43.040
Lynga will not lose!

08:43.040 --> 08:45.840
I will etch my sublime nudity into your eyes!

08:46.340 --> 08:48.500
All of you...

08:49.010 --> 08:51.670
Go to the women's bath!

08:52.260 --> 08:53.360
What was that?

08:54.390 --> 08:58.890
It'd be a shame if there was some 
weirdo who ruined my hot spring trip.

09:00.010 --> 09:02.770
To be sent on a house call to 
Flamme, the city of hot springs...

09:03.430 --> 09:06.220
I wonder if he noticed how tired I was.

09:07.120 --> 09:10.030
Unbelievable. The three 
of you are just shameless!

09:10.730 --> 09:12.610
I don't buy that, coming from you.

09:13.120 --> 09:16.310
Not that I didn't know it already, 
but the doc's no fun.

09:16.310 --> 09:18.490
Lynga thinks he's just embarrassed.

09:18.490 --> 09:22.370
I was hoping to display 
more of my grand nude form!

09:22.370 --> 09:27.750
<i>Kind of surprising to see a mixed group 
like that bathing together socially.</i>

09:28.940 --> 09:31.000
You need something?

09:31.000 --> 09:34.900
Oh, excuse me! It's nothing, sorry.

09:34.900 --> 09:35.800
If you say so.

09:36.380 --> 09:39.710
She was likely entranced by my proportions!

09:39.710 --> 09:42.710
To enchant even other women... 
How wicked must my body be?

09:42.710 --> 09:47.140
Lynga sometimes wonders where 
your confidence comes from.

09:47.950 --> 09:49.390
I'm jealous.

09:50.650 --> 09:51.890
<i>She's adorable!</i>

09:53.850 --> 10:00.140
Maybe if I had a nicer body, I could've 
charged into the men's bath more confidently.

10:00.140 --> 10:01.180
"Charged"?

10:01.620 --> 10:04.170
Everyone else's chests are so big.

10:04.170 --> 10:06.750
And mine... isn't!

10:23.750 --> 10:25.770
There's no need to be pessimistic.

10:25.770 --> 10:28.270
You're still growing, after all.

10:28.270 --> 10:31.920
And there's no guarantee that 
bigger is the preferred size.

10:32.820 --> 10:36.860
Is that true?! Even if they're 
small, he might still like them?

10:38.590 --> 10:44.740
Indeed! There are depths to this world 
that children have trouble imagining.

10:44.740 --> 10:47.420
The world of depths...

10:47.420 --> 10:50.070
The world of small chests!

10:50.070 --> 10:54.830
Huh? Carmilla, you seem more 
transparent than usual.

10:54.830 --> 10:58.010
It's so pleasant, I may be 
on the verge of ascending.

10:58.010 --> 11:02.400
Oh, I'm vanishing! I'm vanishing!

11:00.460 --> 11:02.400
Oh, no! Don't go!

11:02.400 --> 11:03.760
A joke, of course.

11:04.150 --> 11:06.890
Don't scare me like that!

11:06.890 --> 11:09.270
<i>Is that... a wraith?!</i>

11:10.020 --> 11:12.600
Root of all life, by your blessing...

11:12.600 --> 11:15.480
Oh, dear! It seems there are other guests here!

11:17.610 --> 11:19.170
Whoa, you scared me!

11:19.170 --> 11:21.240
You're in on this now, too, Carmilla?!

11:21.240 --> 11:24.120
You seem upset. Shall I rinse you off?

11:24.120 --> 11:25.740
You want me to exorcise you?!

11:26.240 --> 11:28.500
Did I... imagine that?

11:29.040 --> 11:32.460
I must really be exhausted.

11:34.660 --> 11:37.420
Doc, here's to more than one job done well!

11:37.840 --> 11:38.950
Cheers!

11:38.950 --> 11:40.550
Cheers!

11:42.090 --> 11:43.800
It looks so good!

11:46.190 --> 11:50.000
Krishna, if you're gonna make 
that face, why not just join us?

11:51.310 --> 11:54.060
That's right! Come join us!

11:54.400 --> 11:57.770
For a guardian of order to be 
put in this kind of situation...

11:57.770 --> 12:04.230
I only took a single day of leave and 
find myself here with all of you!

12:04.230 --> 12:07.020
The idea of toasting 
around the same table...

12:07.020 --> 12:09.040
Sounds like your whole thing is complicated.

12:09.040 --> 12:10.910
By the way, where's Carmilla?

12:11.260 --> 12:15.220
"I will take my drink in my room, 
where I can relax," she said.

12:21.450 --> 12:22.800
I'm back.

12:23.390 --> 12:25.010
And I'm tired...

12:25.010 --> 12:27.560
Was the meal not an enjoyable one?

12:27.560 --> 12:29.810
It was, at first.

12:29.810 --> 12:34.560
But then they started a drinking game where 
the winner was supposed to sit on my lap...

12:40.890 --> 12:44.160
Wasn't the whole point of all 
this to help with my exhaustion?

12:44.160 --> 12:46.780
Oh, it's fine.

12:46.780 --> 12:50.160
Enjoy the lively times while they last.

12:50.740 --> 12:54.660
I'm sure you're going to be drawn into 
more complicated matters soon enough.

12:54.660 --> 12:56.990
Could you please stop jinxing me?

12:57.960 --> 13:00.800
A wraith's intuition tends to be accurate.

13:00.800 --> 13:03.930
How did you get here, anyway?

13:03.930 --> 13:06.680
I thought you couldn't be 
out in the sun for long.

13:06.680 --> 13:07.900
With that.

13:08.560 --> 13:13.180
Since my body is ethereal, I can 
possess objects I'm attached to.

13:13.180 --> 13:17.440
I inhabited that staff, which 
Lily carried during the day.

13:17.440 --> 13:21.150
If you're attached to it, did it 
belong to you when you were alive?

13:21.550 --> 13:24.760
What were you up to back then, anyway?

13:24.760 --> 13:28.280
It was so long ago that I've forgotten.

13:28.560 --> 13:33.950
Now, given your troubles, 
let me pour you a drink.

13:33.950 --> 13:37.300
You really don't like to talk 
about your past, do you?

13:47.180 --> 13:48.680
What happened?!

13:48.680 --> 13:51.180
My husband said he was going 
to prepare breakfast,

13:51.180 --> 13:54.430
then he went to the kitchen, 
and there was this loud noise...

13:54.430 --> 13:57.810
The fire magic stones may have exploded.

13:57.810 --> 14:00.900
I'm a healer. I'll do what I can.

14:01.710 --> 14:04.780
Root of all life, by your blessing,

14:04.780 --> 14:06.400
grant your amelioration.

14:06.400 --> 14:07.500
Heal!

14:09.160 --> 14:11.520
First aid is the best I can do here.

14:11.520 --> 14:13.540
This will take a while to properly heal.

14:13.540 --> 14:17.630
And in the condition his arm is in, he 
may never be able to hold a knife again.

14:17.630 --> 14:18.650
What happened?

14:19.170 --> 14:20.460
Who are you?

14:20.460 --> 14:21.790
A guest.

14:22.240 --> 14:25.170
I was wondering what that explosion was.

14:25.740 --> 14:26.920
He's burnt?

14:26.920 --> 14:30.290
There's a Royal Hospital branch 
in the center of the city.

14:30.290 --> 14:33.180
They would have more 
advanced healing magic circles.

14:33.180 --> 14:35.560
Can you help me carry him?

14:35.560 --> 14:38.560
Never heard of that stuff 
before. Sounds interesting.

14:38.560 --> 14:40.190
Interesting?

14:40.190 --> 14:42.770
But with these injuries, I doubt he'll need it.

14:44.640 --> 14:46.670
Zenos! What happened?

14:46.670 --> 14:48.950
A bit of a kitchen fire.

14:48.950 --> 14:50.680
Our ride is leaving soon. Let's go.

14:50.680 --> 14:52.280
W-Wait!

14:52.280 --> 14:54.950
The food here was good.
I wouldn't mind eating it again.

14:55.240 --> 14:56.830
So this one's on the house.

14:58.330 --> 15:02.860
Unbelievable. Abandoning 
someone who's injured...

15:03.800 --> 15:05.710
Huh? What happened to me?

15:05.710 --> 15:07.250
Honey!

15:07.250 --> 15:08.340
How?

15:07.250 --> 15:09.900
Thank goodness! I'm so relieved!

15:08.690 --> 15:12.470
<i>Did my spell do that?</i>

15:12.470 --> 15:15.720
<i>No, he was hurt too badly 
for that to be possible.</i>

15:15.720 --> 15:19.810
<i>To treat that kind of burn instantly with 
no magical circle for reinforcement,</i>

15:19.810 --> 15:20.850
<i>he must be highly ranked...</i>

15:20.850 --> 15:24.410
<i>No, only a Saint or an 
elite healer could do that!</i>

15:28.940 --> 15:31.200
And that's the story.

15:31.200 --> 15:36.580
An elite healer capable of restoring 
severe burns in an instant...

15:36.580 --> 15:40.720
Those are valuable. There are less 
than ten of them in the country.

15:40.720 --> 15:43.830
I'm sure the government would 
want him as a national asset.

15:43.830 --> 15:47.440
He left while I was still in shock.

15:47.440 --> 15:50.140
Do you remember what he was like?

15:50.140 --> 15:53.840
He had black hair, but other than that...

15:54.560 --> 15:58.310
I think I remember someone 
calling him "Zenos," though.

15:59.700 --> 16:03.110
That could be an alias, 
so it's not much to go on.

16:03.110 --> 16:07.030
Still, if he healed someone and then 
went on his way, he can't be a bad guy.

16:07.030 --> 16:09.940
I'm sure there's no harm in letting him go.

16:09.940 --> 16:13.600
If anything, running into him again 
would mean we'd have to dig deeper.

16:13.600 --> 16:16.390
I see.

16:16.390 --> 16:21.330
Actually, one other thing I remember 
is that he had a black overcoat.

16:21.650 --> 16:25.780
An elite-grade healer 
with a black overcoat...

16:26.590 --> 16:28.420
I've changed my mind.

16:28.420 --> 16:30.920
Let's search for him after all.

16:30.920 --> 16:32.890
Oh... Okay.

16:32.890 --> 16:34.680
But how?

16:34.680 --> 16:37.020
If he doesn't have official registration,

16:37.020 --> 16:40.060
he may not be a legal citizen.

16:40.060 --> 16:41.710
You think he's from the slums?

16:41.710 --> 16:44.190
That doesn't narrow it down much, though.

16:44.190 --> 16:46.700
Oh, I'm sure we'll manage...

16:48.190 --> 16:50.750
I'm not sure why you're laughing.

16:50.750 --> 16:53.070
Or why you suddenly changed your mind.

16:53.440 --> 16:55.700
I'd just like to meet him.

16:55.700 --> 16:58.030
As a fellow elite healer.

17:00.890 --> 17:03.080
Sorry about this, Doc!

17:04.060 --> 17:05.080
Is he sick?

17:05.080 --> 17:09.920
Don't know him, but he coughed up 
a ton of blood and then collapsed.

17:09.920 --> 17:13.140
It might be contagious, 
so you made the right call.

17:13.140 --> 17:14.670
Lay him down on the bed.

17:21.870 --> 17:24.310
His lungs are a mess...

17:25.730 --> 17:27.190
This is Red Lung!

17:27.190 --> 17:29.030
Red Lung?

17:29.030 --> 17:31.690
Lily, Zonde, back away.

17:32.020 --> 17:34.870
There was a pandemic that killed 
a lot of people a while back.

17:34.870 --> 17:36.190
His case is similar.

17:37.410 --> 17:41.140
But Red Lung was supposed to have 
been wiped out thanks to a cure...

17:41.140 --> 17:42.960
So why would there be a new infection?

17:42.960 --> 17:46.040
Then again, maybe there's 
only a resemblance...

17:46.040 --> 17:50.600
I must say, that was quite the diagnosis.

17:52.870 --> 17:56.560
It's nice to meet you, underground 
healer from the abandoned district.

17:56.560 --> 18:00.800
I'm an elite healer from the 
Royal Hospital, Ernardo Becker.

18:01.170 --> 18:04.040
You're an elite healer 
with the Royal Hospital?

18:04.040 --> 18:07.010
Correct, although my case 
is a bit unique in that

18:07.010 --> 18:10.310
I'm not particularly good with healing magic.

18:10.310 --> 18:13.220
Wait, then do you actually have Red Lung?

18:13.220 --> 18:14.940
It seemed a little different.

18:14.940 --> 18:16.240
Oh, that...

18:16.240 --> 18:17.950
Dr. Becker!

18:20.070 --> 18:22.580
Oh, the healer from before!

18:20.070 --> 18:22.580
Hey, it's the girl from the inn.

18:22.580 --> 18:24.170
Hello there, Umin!

18:24.170 --> 18:26.450
Don't you "Hello there, Umin" me!

18:26.450 --> 18:29.040
Do you realize how crazy it is 
to make yourself seriously sick

18:29.040 --> 18:31.840
and then ask me to follow you 
when you're taken to this clinic?!

18:31.840 --> 18:34.380
Well, how else were we supposed to find him?

18:36.550 --> 18:39.430
You know, I thought I had 
weakened it enough,

18:39.430 --> 18:42.140
but it's still quite painful.

18:42.800 --> 18:45.090
What's causing your symptoms?

18:46.690 --> 18:50.940
I took a drug that would cause 
symptoms similar to Red Lung.

18:51.210 --> 18:54.220
The locals are quite cautious,

18:54.220 --> 18:58.320
but I thought they'd be willing 
to help someone seriously ill.

18:58.320 --> 19:02.170
The effects wear off quickly, so I won't die.

19:02.170 --> 19:05.700
I also took a dose of the antidote to 
be on the safe side, so I'll be fine.

19:05.700 --> 19:08.780
Where in the world did you 
find a drug like that?

19:08.780 --> 19:11.300
I made it myself.

19:11.300 --> 19:15.920
It became a necessity in my efforts 
to come up with a cure for Red Lung.

19:15.920 --> 19:19.850
The cure for Red Lung? Then you're—

19:19.850 --> 19:21.300
That's right!

19:21.300 --> 19:23.490
Red Lung, the Thousand-Day 
Cough, Crimson Poison!

19:23.490 --> 19:26.790
Dr. Becker has come up with treatments 
for a number of diseases,

19:26.790 --> 19:30.940
and was awarded the special rank of 
elite healer for his efforts! He's amazing!

19:33.420 --> 19:35.820
It was really nothing special.

19:36.410 --> 19:40.080
When I heard about an elite-class 
healer in a black overcoat,

19:40.080 --> 19:43.030
I thought it might've been 
someone I used to know...

19:43.030 --> 19:44.420
But it seems I was wrong.

19:45.450 --> 19:48.200
That coat is yours, I assume?

19:48.200 --> 19:51.420
Yeah. But it originally 
belonged to my teacher.

19:51.420 --> 19:52.980
What was your teacher's name?

19:52.980 --> 19:56.420
Don't know. Never actually told me.

19:58.880 --> 20:02.930
Umin, why don't we bring him 
in on this case after all?

20:03.690 --> 20:05.030
Are you sure?

20:05.030 --> 20:06.430
What case?

20:07.920 --> 20:10.310
I know this is sudden, Zenos,

20:10.310 --> 20:13.000
but would you like to work 
at the Royal Hospital?

20:14.180 --> 20:17.070
We're dealing with a bit of a problem, you see.

20:17.070 --> 20:19.890
Why would you ask a total 
stranger like me for help?

20:19.890 --> 20:21.700
It's a rather delicate issue,

20:21.700 --> 20:24.450
the kind where an outsider would 
have an easier time taking action.

20:25.980 --> 20:26.950
You guys!

20:26.950 --> 20:29.230
What are you all doing here?

20:29.230 --> 20:32.830
The red flag was up, so we rushed down here.

20:32.830 --> 20:34.140
The flag?

20:34.140 --> 20:36.580
Oh, red is for emergencies.

20:36.910 --> 20:39.300
Carmilla must've noticed something was up.

20:39.300 --> 20:42.170
I'd like to see you try and take Doc away!

20:42.170 --> 20:45.590
Sir Zenos forbids fighting in the clinic,

20:45.590 --> 20:47.940
so we won't hurt you in here.

20:47.940 --> 20:50.270
But take one step outside the building,

20:50.270 --> 20:53.560
and our men might take 
offense with your actions.

20:55.160 --> 20:59.150
This display of unity as 
you all try to protect him!

20:59.150 --> 21:02.820
I wonder if any healer has ever 
accomplished anything like it!

21:02.820 --> 21:07.000
I think we might need to 
reconsider our approach.

21:07.530 --> 21:11.950
Let's make this an official deal... 
or rather, a commission.

21:13.240 --> 21:15.270
Yeah, all right.

21:15.270 --> 21:17.460
Doc? You sure about this?

21:17.460 --> 21:21.670
Now that they know about my underground 
operation, I need them on my side.

21:21.970 --> 21:24.280
And I still remember how the central hospital

21:24.280 --> 21:27.650
distributed the cure for 
Red Lung freely in the slums

21:27.650 --> 21:30.680
back when it was spreading, 
saving a lot of lives.

21:30.680 --> 21:31.990
That's right!

21:31.990 --> 21:35.520
There was a lot of opposition, but Dr. Becker 
insisted that, to eradicate the disease,

21:35.520 --> 21:37.760
the cure had to be distributed to everyone,

21:37.760 --> 21:40.250
and he went as far as to pay for it himself!

21:40.250 --> 21:44.690
I was only taking the appropriate 
scientific approach.

21:46.230 --> 21:48.820
That was a big help, yeah.

21:49.150 --> 21:52.990
More importantly, you seem to know my teacher.

21:52.990 --> 21:58.500
If you agree to come to the Royal Hospital, 
I'll give you more details in time.

21:58.500 --> 22:02.160
You called it a commission, 
but now you're bargaining again.

22:02.160 --> 22:04.630
You're a crafty one, aren't you?

22:04.630 --> 22:06.290
I've been called that.

22:06.290 --> 22:09.150
I'm sure the same can be said of you.

22:09.150 --> 22:12.590
I'm just trying to live life the 
way I like it, which is quietly.

22:13.680 --> 22:15.370
Once this matter is taken care of,

22:15.370 --> 22:17.480
you'll have my assistance in that regard.

22:17.930 --> 22:18.990
To make it official:

22:19.520 --> 22:23.830
Welcome to the Royal Hospital, 
Zenos the underground healer.

23:55.540 --> 24:00.000
The Royal Hospital

23:57.170 --> 23:58.700
"The Royal Hospital."
